  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on small probability outcomes (less than 20%) and adjusts their weights upward by 10 percentage points. In Lottery A, the 0 Euro outcome has a 55% probability and the -6000 Euro outcome has 45%; neither is below 20%, so no adjustment applies. In Lottery B, the 0 Euro outcome has 10% probability (which is below 20%), so its weight is increased to 20% (10% + 10%), and the -3000 Euro outcome has 90%, which remains unchanged. The reason evaluates the weighted sum of outcomes, with special emphasis on low-probability events. Since there is one outcome below 20% (the 0 Euro in B), the adjustment applies only to that. The adjusted expected value under the reason would give more weight to the 0 Euro outcome in B, potentially making B more favorable under this distorted weighting. Thus, the reason can meaningfully distinguish between the lotteries based on overweighting rare outcomes.",
