  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying outcomes with less than 20% probability and increasing their weight by 10 percentage points, then comparing the weighted sums. In this case, only the 0 Euro outcome in Lottery B qualifies as a low-probability event (10%). The reason would involve adjusting its weight and re-evaluating the lotteries accordingly. However, the individual’s report shows no mention of such a process. Instead, they focused exclusively on the probability of a loss occurring, preferring the lottery with the lower chance of any loss. This is a probability-minimization heuristic focused on loss occurrence, not a distortion or overweighting of rare outcomes. There is no evidence that the individual attended to outcomes with less than 20% probability or adjusted their weights. The justification is based on a different principle: avoid the higher chance of loss. Therefore, the mechanism and information use of the decision reason are not reflected in the verbal report.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
